Dangling prompt bug(?) when playing DOS version of NetHack v343 on WinXP




Symptom: 

  "In what direction?" prompt remains on first line of screen
  after pressing <ESC> during "(a)pply tool".  

  Can cause player to move/attack in the direction s/he thinks 
  the tool will be applied in. 

  And end up in the water on Juiblex level.  Several times.  
  Because^W IF s/he is a slow learner.


Cause: 

  Pressing <ESC> after a(pplying) a directional tool.


Example:

  <abbreviated inventory>
  Tools
  a - an uncursed looking glass

  Command entered: "a"pply

  "What do you want to use or apply?..." prompt appears
     on first line of screen

  Command entered: "a"      <Inventory item a - an uncursed looking glass>

  "In what direction?" prompt comes up on first line of screen, 
  with cursor position almost immediately after it.

  Press <ESC>.

  Prompt remains, but cursor returns to player-character symbol.

  Pressing a direction key causes player to move/attack in that
    direction, not apply the tool in that direction.




Notes: 

  Pressing <ESC> again does clear the prompt.

v343 Buglist:


  There's only one occurrence of "prompt" in 
  <http://www.nethack.org/v343/bugs.html>, for C343-11:

  If you ask for help ('?') at a "what direction" prompt, 
  you don't get to enter a direction afterward if the 
  cmdassist option is set.

No occurrences of "tool" or "appl" in the v343 bugs list.



Speculation: 

  Did the "apply" command formerly return to the 
  "What do you want to use or apply?..." prompt when <ESC>
  was pressed during the directional phase?



